{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_NUfjwOVo5mQQagHyyVrPCeDG","content":"1\t# What GND supports\n2\t\n3\tGND combines a conceptual model, deterministic checks, and agent workflows\n4\tfor building applications around explicit domain rules. Choose a capability\n5\tby the question you need to answer. The supported fragment differs between\n6\tchecking, generation, measurement, and external exports.\n7\t\n8\tThe tutorials exercise local Python/CLI paths with synthetic public inputs.\n9\tAn available command is not by itself a measured support claim for every\n10\toperating system, Python version, provider, or native toolchain. See the\n11\t[compatibility policy](../compatibility.md) for release support.\n12\t\n13\t## Capabilities by task\n14\t\n15\t| Task | Supported surface | Principal boundary | Start here |\n16\t|---|---|---|---|\n17\t| Describe a domain and its rules | ORM YAML/JSON; guided text-to-model skill; readable verbalization | A person reviews requirements and inferred constraints | [Modeling](../guides/modeling.md) |\n18\t| Validate a model | CLI `validate`; `api.validate` | Valid syntax/semantics do not establish complete requirements | [Python API](python-api.md) |\n19\t| Check candidate facts | `check`; `api.check`; admission projection | Checks supplied facts and declared coverage; no automatic repair | [Quickstart](../quickstart.md) |\n20\t| Explain supplied facts | `verbalize population`; `api.verbalize` | Deterministic sentences are not a truth judgment | [Python API](python-api.md) |\n21\t| Explain a missing derived fact | `why-not`; `api.why_not` | Declared-order steps and the first empty one; counts values spelled differently; no aggregates or prose rules; values redacted by default | [Why-not](why-not.md) |\n22\t| Serve internal or customer readers | `GND_DISCLOSURE`, `--disclosure` | Customer mode refuses requests for values; a guard, not a lock, for code inside the process; some outputs are the same in every mode | [Disclosure](disclosure.md) |\n23\t| Compute derived relations | Structured clauses, joins, supported exact terms, stratified negation, recursion and aggregates | Resource bounds and construct-specific validation apply | [Data and transitions](../guides/data-and-transitions.md) |\n24\t| Check calendar deadlines | Date/Duration guarded comparisons | Calendar days only; no live clock, timezones, or business calendar | [Data and transitions](../guides/data-and-transitions.md) |\n25\t| Use a fixed catalog | Version-4 reference populations with path and byte-hash binding | Candidate/reference fact ownership is disjoint | [Data and transitions](../guides/data-and-transitions.md) |\n26\t| Audit an operation walk | `check --pre --steps --post`; `api.transition` | Frame checks cover the walk's touched fact types | [Python API](python-api.md) |\n27\t| Reuse a checked pre-state | `api.check_with_receipt`; `api.transition(pre_receipt=...)` | In-process, default options; only the pre-state check is skipped | [Python API](python-api.md#reusing-a-checked-pre-state) |\n28\t| Recheck related snapshots | `api.EvaluationSession` | Explicit loaded-input session; conservative fresh fallback, one bounded generation, full snapshot validation | [Python API](python-api.md#reusing-evaluation-work-across-snapshots) |\n29\t| Incorporate host observations | `EvaluationSession.observe`, `check_with_feedback` | Validated relation replacement; counts are diagnostic, not external truth; separate in-process feedback wire | [Host loop](../agents/dev-session.md#a-host-loop-in-one-python-process) |\n30\t| Generate a Python project | `codegen` plus explicitly selected skill | Developer writes extension behavior; temporal models refused | [Generated projects](../guides/generated-projects.md) |\n31\t| Detect model/project drift | `conformance`; static architecture checks | Does not execute the app or verify all extension behavior | [Generated projects](../guides/generated-projects.md) |\n32\t| Change an existing model | Staged `evolve preview/apply/finalize` | Explicit reviewed changes; no automatic regeneration | [Evolution](../guides/evolution-and-recovery.md) |\n33\t| Discover rules in data | `discover` over one population | Proposes induced, advisory rules only; admission is a reviewed evolve step; single-role families, stated bounds; opt-in `fact-type` family proposes fact types from a declared generic fact type, rendering the `gnd-judge-fact-types` and `gnd-model-multivalued` skills' verdicts when given | [Discovery](discover.md) |\n34\t| Recover a model from code | Bounded `recovery inventory/verify` and authoring skill | One-time static selected roots; no continuous synchronization | [Recovery](../guides/evolution-and-recovery.md) |\n35\t| Compare compatible models | `diff`; `api.diff` | Same vocabulary; bounded entailment catalogue and concrete populations; no temporal models | [Python API](python-api.md) |\n36\t| Exercise rule behavior | `synth`, `measure` | Optional synth dependency; generation is narrower than checking | [Synthetic data](../guides/synthetic-data.md) |\n37\t| Measure rules on your own labels | `measure --labels` | Host-labelled populations; expected-state rates or class agreement counts; labels are your claim, not checked truth | [Measuring host labels](measure-labels.md) |\n38\t| Learn rules with an ILP learner or rule miner | `export ilp`, `import ilp-rules`, `import mined-rules`; the `gnd-induce` skill runs them with an assistant | GND runs no learner; adapters `popper`, `neutral`, `ilasp`, `llm`, `rules` (labelled) and `amie` (unlabelled); learned clauses in a declared fragment become induced, advisory guarded constraints only when GND's own count equals the learner's, and mined rules only when they also hold for every case; each learner's rendering was run against one real learner version, one run per approved setting (`neutral` through the language-model run) ([comparison](../how-to/compare-ilp-learners.md)) | [ILP bridge](ilp-bridge.md) |\n39\t| Extract and check document facts | Offline extraction bundle, agent skill, `verify`, source anchors | Agent performs extraction; checking is distinct from fidelity | [Documents](../guides/documents.md) |\n40\t| Render evaluation documents | Agent rendering skill, `doccheck`, `fidelity` | Bound manifests and distractors; fidelity remains a separate measured claim | [Documents](../guides/documents.md) |\n41\t| Run a bounded agent experiment | `exp` commands and selected adapter/policy | Requires authored contract; live adapter prerequisites are separate | [Experiments](../guides/experiments.md) |\n42\t| Evaluate saved external opinions | `judgments check`; explicit session judgment gate | Consumes receipts; does not obtain opinions or calibrate providers | [Experiments](../guides/experiments.md) |\n43\t| Compose several documents' facts | `compose`, `check --composition --sources`; API compose | Explicit manifest renamings only; re-derived on check; each anchored value checked in its own document; lineage proves no truth | [Composition](composition.md), [how-to](../how-to/compose-documents.md) |\n44\t| Explain a finite derived tuple | `witness`, `replay`, `witness-view`; API witness/replay; `--composition` for source lineage | Selected positive proof fragment, not extension completeness | [Exports](../guides/exports.md) |\n45\t| Export to external runtimes | Bounded Souffle/Lean/PyRel profiles | Export, native execution, compilation and proof are distinct | [Exports](../guides/exports.md), [worked native guides](../runtimes/scenario.md) |\n46\t| Review a plan or result | Explicit advisory review-panel skill and CLI | Live tools/credentials; reviewer findings do not apply fixes | [Exports and a second opinion](../agents/export-and-review.md) |\n47\t\n48\t## Constraint coverage\n49\t\n50\t| Family | What checking supports |\n51\t|---|---|\n52\t| Uniqueness | Internal role combinations and external identifiers |\n53\t| Mandatory | Individual roles and inclusive-or participation over the declared instance set |\n54\t| Values | Enumerations, ranges, multiple ranges and supported role-scoped forms |\n55\t| Frequency | Internal and external occurrence bounds |\n56\t| Relational inclusion | Subset and equality over declared role sequences |\n57\t| Exclusion and partitions | Exclusion; exclusive-or, with only the exclusion component for multi-role sequences |\n58\t| Ring properties | Thirteen variants; each has its own local relation semantics |\n59\t| Comparison | Supported typed comparisons; current-time operands remain unchecked |\n60\t| Cardinality | Object and role counts |\n61\t| Subtype partition | Checks when required membership is observable; otherwise unchecked |\n62\t| Guarded rules | Bound antecedents with supported relation, comparison or absence consequences |\n63\t| Source anchoring | Bound document spans and supported lexical/numeric/date matching |\n64\t| Textual requirements | Preserved, but reported unchecked by the deterministic checker |\n65\t\n66\tThe [constraint reference](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/blob/main/src/gnd/skills/gnd-orm-core/references/constraint-reference.md)\n67\tis the detailed authority for syntax and semantics. “Supported” does not mean\n68\tevery downstream tool accepts every combination of these constructs.\n69\t\n70\t## Compatibility between feature families\n71\t\n72\tTemporal models currently work in validation and documented check/transition\n73\tsurfaces, including the packaged dispatch admission example. They are refused\n74\tby synth, measure, codegen, conformance, diff, extraction, document checking,\n75\tand the existing PyRel exporter. Date values alone do not necessarily select\n76\ttemporal arithmetic; `Duration` and temporal terms do.\n77\t\n78\tNative proof/export profiles have separate restrictions. The witness lane\n79\tdoes not admit negation or aggregates; Souffle exports exclude constraints\n80\tand operations; Lean uses a selected finite acyclic fragment. Unsupported\n81\tinput is not silently converted to a successful partial export.\n82\t\n83\t## What an application still provides\n84\t\n85\tGND does not supply a hosted application, database, UI, deployment service,\n86\tuniversal optimizer, or recommender ranking-quality guarantee. Your code\n87\tdecides how to obtain facts, propose outputs, persist state, and present\n88\tfindings. The model states what those outputs must satisfy.\n89\t\n90\tMechanical verdicts, model/project conformance, experiment acceptance,\n91\textraction fidelity, advisory review, and formal assurance are different\n92\tresults. A pass in one does not automatically confer the others. Missing or\n93\tstale assurance evidence remains unavailable; the documentation tutorials\n94\tdo not perform certification or recertification."}
