{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_ijghfeZ1QYVsQl9kN7Rt8ufl","content":"1\t\"\"\"Render a model's rules as a readable PyRel program, as requirements.\n2\t\n3\tEvery supported constraint becomes one :class:`Requirement`: a *domain* (the\n4\tfacts the rule talks about) and a *check* (what must hold for each of them).\n5\tThat is PyRel's own shape for a logical rule, ``m.where(<domain>).require(<check>)``.\n6\t\n7\tTwo programs are rendered from the same list:\n8\t\n9\t``lqp``\n10\t    Each rule is an executable ``require``. A RelationalAI engine (the logic\n11\t    reasoner, \"LQP\") enforces it and reports every violation. Requirements are\n12\t    not enforced by the local DuckDB backend, so this program does not check\n13\t    anything locally; ``--compile`` shows how PyRel compiled each requirement.\n14\t\n15\t``duckdb``\n16\t    Each rule is printed as the same ``require`` and evaluated in its denial\n17\t    form, ``m.where(<domain>, <not check>)``: the facts that would violate it.\n18\t    The logic reasoner's direct LQP compiler lowers a requirement to that same\n19\t    condition (``domain and not check => Error``), so both programs state one rule.\n20\t\n21\tThe checker that GND's applications run (``pyrel_runtime.py``) is separate;\n22\t``tests/test_pyrel_rules.py`` ties the two by agreement.\n23\t\"\"\"\n24\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n25\t\n26\timport datetime as _dt\n27\timport json\n28\timport keyword\n29\timport re\n30\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field, replace\n31\tfrom pathlib import Path\n32\tfrom typing import Any\n33\t\n34\tfrom gnd.errors import ModelLoadError, ModelValidationError\n35\tfrom gnd.graphs import strongly_connected_components\n36\tfrom gnd.model import iter_derivation_clauses, load_model_bytes\n37\tfrom gnd.model_index import ModelIndex\n38\tfrom gnd.terms import (\n39\t    MEMBERSHIP_OPERATORS,\n40\t    compile_membership,\n41\t    guard_uses_membership,\n42\t    guarded_clause_refusal,\n43\t    where_uses_membership,\n44\t)\n45\t\n46\tfrom .pyrel_runtime import ExportInputError, _parse_document\n47\t\n48\tTARGETS = (\"duckdb\", \"lqp\")\n49\tPYREL_VERSION = \"1.30.1\"\n50\t# model primitive -> PyRel type; a Duration is a whole number of days (GND has no other durations)\n51\t_TYPES = {\"String\": \"String\", \"Integer\": \"Integer\", \"Float\": \"Float\", \"Boolean\": \"Boolean\", \"Date\": \"Date\",\n52\t          \"Duration\": \"Integer\", \"Number\": \"Float\"}   # D2: GND's Number admits what Float admits\n53\t_BINARY = {\"Float\", \"Number\"}   # model types the programs hold as binary floats\n54\t_EXACT_FLOAT = 2**53            # D6: every integer up to this magnitude is exact as a binary float\n55\t\n56\t\n57\tdef _binary_variables(model: _Model, atoms: Any) -> set[str]:\n58\t    \"\"\"Every variable that fills a Float or Number role in any of the atoms, whatever its other roles.\"\"\"\n59\t    found: set[str] = set()\n60\t    for atom in atoms:\n61\t        for role, arg in zip(model.roles(atom.relation), atom.args):\n62\t            if isinstance(arg, str) and arg.startswith(\"$\") and model.raw_role_type(atom.relation, role[\"role_name\"]) in _BINARY:\n63\t                found.add(arg)\n64\t    return found\n65\t\n66\t\n67\tdef _refuse_binary_context(context: str, terms: Any, binary: set[str], *, always: bool = False) -> None:\n68\t    \"\"\"D6: where a Float or Number value takes part, every constant must be exact as a binary float, and no\n69\t    arithmetic may compute one: PyRel would compute it in binary, GND computes it exactly.\"\"\"\n70\t    if not always and not any(v in binary for t in terms for v in _term_variables(t)):\n71\t        return\n72\t    for term in terms:\n73\t        if isinstance(term, dict) and term.get(\"fn\") in _ARITHMETIC:\n74\t            raise ExportInputError(f\"{context}arithmetic next to a Float or Number value is exact in GND and binary \"\n75\t                                   \"in PyRel; the rules programs refuse it\")\n76\t  